<h1>SecureU — Student Safety &amp; Grievance Redressal System</h1>
<p><strong>Course / Purpose:</strong> Java Project / DBMS Lab Documentation</p>
<p><strong>Architecture:</strong> Java Desktop Application (JDK 27) + MySQL JDBC + Native HTTP REST API + Responsive Web Interface</p>
<hr/>

<h2>1. System Requirements & Prerequisites</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Component</th>
      <th>Required Version</th>
      <th>Default Path / Port</th>
      <th>Status Check</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Java Development Kit (JDK)</strong></td>
      <td>JDK 17, 21, or 27</td>
      <td><code>C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-27.0.1.0.3\bin</code></td>
      <td><code>& "C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-27.0.1.0.3\bin\java.exe" -version</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>MySQL Server</strong></td>
      <td>MySQL 5.7+ / 8.0+ (via XAMPP)</td>
      <td>Port <code>3306</code></td>
      <td>Check XAMPP Control Panel (Green status)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Web Browser</strong></td>
      <td>Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Brave</td>
      <td><code>http://localhost:3000</code></td>
      <td>Any modern HTML5 browser</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. Step-by-Step Instructions to Start Local Server</h2>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Step 1: Start MySQL Database (XAMPP)</strong>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <strong>XAMPP Control Panel</strong> on your computer.</li>
    <li>Click the <strong>Start</strong> button next to <strong>MySQL</strong>.</li>
    <li>Ensure the MySQL module shows a green background with port <strong>3306</strong> active.</li>
    <li><em>(First-time only)</em>: Open <a href="http://localhost/phpmyadmin">http://localhost/phpmyadmin</a> in your browser. If the database <code>CollegeComplaint</code> is not created yet, import the SQL script located at <code>sql/CollegeComplaint.sql</code>. (The Java backend also automatically verifies and seeds sample tables if needed).</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Step 2: Launch the Java Server</strong>
  <p>Choose <strong>ONE</strong> of the following options:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Option A (One-Click Launcher - Recommended):</strong><br>
      In the project folder, simply double-click <strong><code>Launch-CollegeComplaint.bat</code></strong>.<br>
      <em>Note: It automatically terminates any old background process holding port 3000 and launches the application cleanly.</em>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Option B (PowerShell Terminal):</strong><br>
      If <code>java</code> is not recognized in your terminal, run with the full path:
      <pre>& "C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-27.0.1.0.3\bin\java.exe" -jar CollegeComplaint.jar</pre>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Option C (Alternative Node.js Server):</strong><br>
      If PowerShell blocks <code>npm.ps1</code> script execution, run <code>node server.js</code> or <code>npm.cmd start</code>:
      <pre>node server.js</pre>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Step 3: Open the Web Portal in Your Browser</strong>
  <p>Navigate to:</p>
  <pre>http://localhost:3000</pre>
</div>

