      <td>Hostel grievance management, update status (Pending / Under Review / Resolved), add redressal remarks, preview attached evidence.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>HOD</strong></td>
      <td><code>hod.cse@example.com</code></td>
      <td><code>hod@123</code></td>
      <td>Academic and departmental grievance oversight, view resolution analytics charts, update complaints, review evidence.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>4. Solutions to Common Terminal Errors</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Terminal Error</th>
      <th>Why It Happens</th>
      <th>Exact Fix</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong><code>Address already in use: bind</code></strong></td>
      <td>A previous Java server instance was still running on port 3000.</td>
      <td>Double-click <code>Launch-CollegeComplaint.bat</code> (auto-cleans port 3000) or run <code>taskkill /F /IM java.exe</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong><code>The term 'java' is not recognized</code></strong></td>
      <td>The current terminal session was opened before PATH was refreshed.</td>
      <td>Run: <code>& "C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-27.0.1.0.3\bin\java.exe" -jar CollegeComplaint.jar</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong><code>npm.ps1 cannot be loaded because running scripts is disabled</code></strong></td>
      <td>Windows PowerShell restricts <code>.ps1</code> script execution by default.</td>
      <td>Run: <code>node server.js</code> or <code>npm.cmd start</code></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<hr/>
<p style="text-align: center; color: #737373; font-size: 9pt;">CollegeComplaint — Grievance Redressal Portal • Generated Documentation</p>

